    {
      "id": "claim_a14b91baaa1b445c933f7b9043b089f1",
      "statement": "lib/match/findOrphanedMatches.ts is a thin service-role wrapper that invokes supabase.rpc(\"find_orphaned_matches\"), returns the ids as a string[] (mapping null data to an empty array), and throws when the RPC reports an error; the detection logic lives entirely in Postgres.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/match/findOrphanedMatches.ts#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7713db302b8cbbf841728f0ee8370c8cc2dc74017863062c5900fc6d265f7998:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ac7ac3a771d442f8918b1819e279280d",
      "statement": "The POST /api/cron/sweep-stale-matches route is guarded by CRON_SECRET: it returns 500 if CRON_SECRET is unset and 401 if the request's Authorization header does not equal `Bearer <CRON_SECRET>`, and orphan detection never runs for an unauthorized request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/cron/sweep-stale-matches/route.ts#L8-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66e7275cef989698330a4bcbbcb37fc37d18bee02d6becc5e8867b2fb89675c3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c78ca94e2dff46e9be24e43d0e5cc8c3",
      "statement": "The sweep route calls findOrphanedMatches() then finalizes each returned match by calling completeMatchInternal(id, \"abandoned\") under Promise.allSettled, so a single failing match does not abort the batch; it returns 200 with { swept, failed } and emits a structured sweep_stale_matches log with swept_count, failed_count, and duration_ms. If detection throws it logs sweep_stale_matches.find_failed and returns 500.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/cron/sweep-stale-matches/route.ts#L25-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:22b4b3f4c973cf2e4bf689fa444bdcd46317ca07ccda5868d47bfc789edad24f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7019cbaf2a9a40d09364d23d969e5589",
      "statement": "completeMatchInternal is idempotent — it short-circuits when the match is already in state 'completed' — and for reason 'abandoned' it records no winner, skips Elo rating changes, resets both players to available, and writes a match.abandoned log, making a concurrent client completion and a sweep pass safe to race.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/actions/match/completeMatch.ts#L100-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:313614826f484cb766abe29dcc797535f2f80c9a8737128fe26de6b6ca4dac03:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f2a149860fda4efd8fca8e3299ae4704",
      "statement": "The sweep migration schedules the job via a guarded do-block that creates the pg_cron and pg_net extensions, unschedules any prior job named 'sweep-stale-matches', and registers cron.schedule('sweep-stale-matches', '*/30 * * * * *', ...) whose body issues net.http_post to current_setting('app.app_url', true) || '/api/cron/sweep-stale-matches' with an Authorization Bearer header built from current_setting('app.cron_secret', true).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://supabase/migrations/20260424001_sweep_stale_matches.sql#L47-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:478b02b550322a3e931d5c8ee738bb3e69912764f1fed6666d1bf0ce3dbabdc3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d3274fa0e57489f9496c17f8e1035a1",
      "statement": "The pg_cron schedule block is safe in environments without pg_cron/pg_net: exception handlers (undefined_file and a catch-all) merely raise a notice so the migration still applies, and because the schedule body reads settings with current_setting(..., true) unset app.app_url/app.cron_secret resolve to NULL so net.http_post no-ops instead of firing; find_orphaned_matches() remains available for direct invocation on any stack.",
      "evidence": [
